Long, long ago (around winter of '88, I think), there was a
comprehensive document, I think it was called the Hack Bible or
somesuch. It started off with basic sections, then got into advanced
knowledge and finally outright spoilers. I know it started with the
quote "Toto, I have a feeling we're not in Kansas anymore," and had a
section called "Polymorphing Yourself, and Other Masochistic
Pastimes."

I don't know who originally wrote it, but I did an edit job, bringing
it up to date with version 2.2 or 2.3 (whichever was current then),
and cleaning up the format and typos. Then somebody else took it over
from me. Does anybody still maintain this document?

I *know* that I don't have it online anywhere. I *think* I have a
hardcopy version somewhere in my files, but I am not going to type it
in (it's *big*). But (and I'll probably regret saying this), if
anybody else is insane enough to want to try typing it in and making
it available to the net again, I would be willing to send out a copy
via mail (I will even pay the postage, because I am a nice guy).

What I don't want -- I don't want to be deluged with requests for
information from it. I don't have time to be a reference librarian,
and remember, it's only current through 2.3 at the latest (and I guess
most people are now playing 3.0j). I also will not mail copies to
everybody and his wombat. I also don't want someone thinking he can be
real clever and get me to send him a copy and then keep it to himself
-- if you are serious about making it available, then I'll do my part.
This might be a nice free-time project for an ambitious four or five
people who have not yet discovered that beer and/or sex are more fun
on a Friday night.

So, anybody want to take on the task? You'd make *lots* of friends.
Especially if you could bring it up to date with all the 3.0 features
that I expect to be running into soon... :-)
